<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dhammayangyi Temple</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1170</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Dhammayangyi Temple is the largest temple at Bagan in Myanmar, built around 1170 by King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/narathu">Narathu</a> of the Pagan Kingdom, who according to tradition seized the throne by murdering his father and brother. Its massive brickwork is admired for its precise construction, while its inner passages were later filled with rubble.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dhammayangyi-temple.jpg" alt="Dhammayangyi Temple" width="320" height="179" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Justin Vidamo · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dhammayangyi_Temple_at_Bagan,Myanmar.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
